DTSTART:20261017T000000
DTEND:20261017T000000
UID:4aeba01025d2c3e4f49608b41661e158@jacklondonpark.com
DESCRIPTION:SOLD OUT What can the rocks beneath our feet tell us about the
  history of Sonoma Mountain? Join geologist Nicole Myers for Rocktober at 
 Jack London State Historic Park and explore the fascinating geologic force
 s that have shaped Sonoma Mountain. As part of the Triple Watershed Series
  presented by Sonoma State University’s Center for Environmental Inquiry
 \, this program will focus on the Sonoma Creek watershed and reveal how ro
 cks\, water\, and life are all connected.
LOCATION:Jack London State Historic Park\, 2400 London Ranch Road\, Glen E
 llen\, CA 95442
URL:https://jacklondonpark.com/events/rocktober-2026
